-- חוק דמי מחלה (היעדרות בשל מחלת הורה), התשנ"ד-1993 — sections 1, 3, 4
-- and 4א: up to six days a year an employee may charge to his accrued sick
-- leave for the illness of his parent or his spouse's, a parent being ill
-- who has become wholly dependent on others for daily activities; that the
-- law adds to every other right; and that the State is an employer like any
-- other. The text is laws/sick-pay-parent-law.toml, pinned from the live
-- page of ספר החוקים הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: the takanon's §1.25.3.1 restates §§1 and 3 as its clause
-- 4 and lists the law among its sources. §2's rules on proving the illness
-- and the need for the absence are the Minister's regulations, not pinned.

IMPORT prelude

@desc A parent's illness, as the Parent Illness Law asks about it.
DECLARE `a parent's illness under the Parent Illness Law` HAS
    `the parent became wholly dependent on others for daily activities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse is an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse took the absence under this law` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The illness the checks below ask about.
`a dependent parent, the spouse working and not taking it` MEANS
    `a parent's illness under the Parent Illness Law` WITH
        `the parent became wholly dependent on others for daily activities` IS TRUE
        `the spouse is an employee`                  IS TRUE
        `the spouse took the absence under this law` IS FALSE

§ `חוק דמי מחלה (היעדרות בשל מחלת הורה) — ששה ימים בשנה`

§§ `1`

-- (א): up to six days a year of absence for the illness of his parent or
-- his spouse's, charged to his accrued sick leave, provided his spouse is
-- an employee and did not take the absence under this law — read as the
-- page prints it, and as the takanon's clause 4 repeats it. (ב): parts of
-- days count, as he chooses, by the hours absent against the day's hours.
@ref law:1
GIVEN p IS A `a parent's illness under the Parent Illness Law`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days a year section 1 of the Parent Illness Law gives` p IS
    IF     p's `the parent became wholly dependent on others for daily activities`
       AND p's `the spouse is an employee`
       AND NOT p's `the spouse took the absence under this law`
    THEN 6
    ELSE 0

@ref law:1
GIVEN `hours absent` IS A NUMBER, `hours he would have worked that day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the part of a day section 1(ב) charges` `hours absent` `hours he would have worked that day` IS
    IF `hours he would have worked that day` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE min 1 (`hours absent` DIVIDED BY `hours he would have worked that day`)

#ASSERT `days a year section 1 of the Parent Illness Law gives` `a dependent parent, the spouse working and not taking it` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the part of a day section 1(ב) charges` 2 8 EQUALS 1 DIVIDED BY 4

§§ `3`

-- For §1, a parent is ill who fell ill and became wholly dependent on
-- others for daily activities, as the National Insurance Law defines them.
@ref law:3
GIVEN `fell ill` IS A BOOLEAN, `wholly dependent on others for daily activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ill as section 3 of the Parent Illness Law means` `fell ill` `wholly dependent on others for daily activities` IF
    `fell ill` AND `wholly dependent on others for daily activities`

#ASSERT NOT `ill as section 3 of the Parent Illness Law means` TRUE FALSE

§§ `4`

-- The law adds to an employee's right by law or agreement and takes none
-- away: for a right measured in one number, the larger stands.
@ref law:4
GIVEN `what the law gives` IS A NUMBER, `what the instrument gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what stands under section 4 of the Parent Illness Law` `what the law gives` `what the instrument gives` IS
    max `what the law gives` `what the instrument gives`

#ASSERT `what stands under section 4 of the Parent Illness Law` 6 6 EQUALS 6

§§ `4א`

-- For this law the State as employer is like any other employer.
@ref law:4א
`the Parent Illness Law binds the State as an employer` MEANS TRUE
